CORRECTION (2026-09-01, same day): this commit message asserts that launchd rejected the malformed plist and that the backup was consequently not loaded. That causation is FALSE.

Verified with Apple's own parser, which is the one launchd uses:
  plutil -lint  -> OK        (accepts the '--' inside the XML comment)
  plistlib      -> REJECTS   (not well-formed, line 12 col 21)

launchd would have loaded the file. The backup was not scheduled because the job had been
deliberately unloaded, which is unrelated to the plist's XML.

The FIX stands regardless — invalid XML that a strict parser rejects is a defect, and it
was failing three real tests. Only the causal claim was wrong.

The error is itself the pattern this commit is about: taking a strict parser's verdict as
evidence about a different parser downstream. plistlib was the adjacent signal; plutil was
the authority, one command away.
